Z||000011||Tina||02-27-2001||10:02 PM||||<BR>Please keep in mind,I did this on purpose.<BR>Already had replacement tranny at the shop<BR>(Izusu 5 speed)<BR>And wanted to see what the Muncie could handle before replacing it.<BR>This is my daily driver in the summer.<BR>And the tranny held up just fine until......<P>Last day to drive Fiero before retiring it for the winter.  <P>Beat on it hard and constant at the local streets for a couple of hours.......No problems.. <BR>Stopped at the shop,picked up flatbed.<BR>Then off to private street and after a half an hour of continous burnouts.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1315468&a=9769902&p=33707670"> <BR>VOILA'<BR> <BR>Almost killed myself though.                 <BR>Jumping out of the car, in time to catch the smoke on camera.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>More pic's of tranny damage at <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumIndex?u=1315468&a=10926061" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumIndex?u=1315468&a=10926061</A> <BR>||||reg||1
